   "widgets_values": [
    "image",
    "",
    "",
    "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, a wide shot at blue hour frames a red-and-white lighthouse on a granite headland of the Breton coast, heavy Atlantic waves bursting white against the rocks below. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed as the lantern room flickers on and its beam begins to sweep across the low storm clouds. [Shot 2] At 00:02.500, the camera cuts to a medium close-up of an old lighthouse keeper in a yellow oilskin coat at the top railing, rain streaming down his weathered face; the gruff, low-voiced old man (S1) squints into the wind and says: <d>[French] Elle tiendra encore cette nuit.</d>\n\noverall_soundscape: Strong wind gusts howl around the tower while waves crash and drain back over the rocks. Rain spatters on oilskin fabric and metal railings, and the lantern mechanism hums steadily overhead.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Low sustained cello drones at a slow tempo, joined by a distant solo fiddle melody that swells gently on the cut and fades with the last wave.",
    true,
    "none",
    5,
    "auto",
    "768p",
    1,
    "[]",
    "match"
   ],
